<title>RUSSIA: Russian Orenburgneft oil shares up 19pct.</title>
<headline>Russian Orenburgneft oil shares up 19pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Russian regional oil company AO Orenburgneft rose 19.4 percent on the Russian Trading System on Thursday, climbing to $6.21 at 1130 GMT from $5.20 on Tuesday, when it was last traded.</p>
<p>Over 72,000 shares had changed hands in seven trades. ONAKO oil holding company has the controlling stake in Orenburgneft, based in southern European Russia near the Ural mountains.</p>
<p>The Russian market is in a rally and undervalued regional shares are often top gainers.</p>
<p>--Peter Henderson, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
